# Juno AI Computer Use Agent - Headless Mode Architecture Guide

## Overview

Juno AI Computer Use Agent supports comprehensive headless CLI operations, allowing complete agent functionality without requiring a GUI. This enables automation, scripting, CI/CD integration, and server deployment scenarios.

**Key Features:**

- **Full Computer Use Support** - All 17 Anthropic Computer Use actions available via CLI
- **Automatic Headless Detection** - No need to specify `--headless` flag when using commands
- **Multiple Output Formats** - JSON, YAML, Text, Markdown, Quiet modes
- **Batch Processing** - Execute multiple commands from files or stdin
- **Interactive Mode** - Real-time CLI session with the agent
- **Voice Integration** - CLI voice recording, transcription, and voice-driven queries
- **Daemon Mode** - Background service for continuous monitoring and automation

## Quick Start Guide

### Building & Running

```bash
# Build the CLI executable
cargo build --release --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml

# The executable will be at: target/release/juno
# Or run directly during development:
cargo run --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml -- query "your command"
```

### Installation

```bash
# After building, optionally install to system PATH
cp target/release/juno /usr/local/bin/juno

# Or run directly from project root
./target/release/juno query "test command"
```

### Basic Usage Examples

```bash
# Simple query - automatically runs in headless mode
juno query "Take a screenshot and describe the current screen"

# Voice query - record audio and process with agent
juno voice query --duration 30

# Check agent status
juno agent status

# Run system health check
juno system health --detailed

# Batch processing from file
juno batch commands.txt

# Interactive CLI session
juno interactive

# Daemon mode for continuous automation
juno daemon start --foreground
```

## Architecture Components

### Core Files

- **`src-tauri/src/cli/headless.rs`** - HeadlessRuntime implementation with all execution logic
- **`src-tauri/src/cli/mod.rs`** - Complete CLI argument parsing with 10 main command categories
- **`src-tauri/src/startup.rs`** - Automatic headless detection and initialization
- **`src-tauri/src/constants/cli.rs`** - CLI constants (operations, timeouts, exit codes, verbosity)

### HeadlessRuntime Structure

```rust
pub struct HeadlessRuntime {
    app_handle: AppHandle,
    output_format: OutputFormat,
    verbosity: u8,
    timeout_duration: Duration,
}

pub struct HeadlessResult {
    pub success: bool,
    pub output: String,
    pub error: Option<String>,
    pub execution_time: Duration,
    pub agent_state: Option<String>,
    pub screenshot: Option<String>,
}
```

### Automatic Headless Detection

Headless mode is automatically activated when:

```rust
self.headless || self.has_legacy_flags() || self.command.is_some()
```

**This means:**

- Any subcommand automatically triggers headless mode
- No need to specify `--headless` flag
- Legacy flags (like `--check-accessibility`) also trigger headless mode

## Complete Command Reference

### 1. Query Operations - AI Agent Queries

Execute AI agent queries with full Computer Use capabilities:

```bash
# Basic query
juno query "Take a screenshot and describe what you see"

# Advanced query with specific model
juno --verbose query "Open Safari and search for AI news" --model claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022

# Query with JSON output for script processing
juno --output json query "Get the current time from the menu bar"

# Continue previous conversation
juno query "Follow up on the previous task" --continue-conversation

# Save transcript
juno query "Analyze this webpage" --save-transcript conversation.txt

# Custom iterations and timeout
juno --timeout 600 query "Complex automation task" --max-iterations 20
```

### 2. Voice Operations - Audio Processing

Voice recording, transcription, and voice-driven queries:

```bash
# Voice query (record and process with agent)
juno voice query --duration 30 --language en

# Record audio to file
juno voice record --duration 60 --output recording.wav --format wav

# Transcribe existing audio file
juno voice transcribe audio.wav --language en --model whisper

# Voice query with conversation continuation
juno voice query --duration 45 --continue-conversation
```

### 3. Dictation Operations - Text Input

Dictation mode for direct text input to applications:

```bash
# Start dictation mode
juno dictation start --target "TextEdit" --language en --auto-punctuation

# Stop active dictation
juno dictation stop

# Check dictation status
juno dictation status

# Configure dictation settings
juno dictation configure --sensitivity 7 --clipboard true --timeout 300
```

### 4. Agent Management

Direct agent control and status monitoring:

```bash
# Get agent status
juno agent status

# Get detailed agent capabilities
juno agent capabilities --detailed

# Start agent monitoring
juno agent monitor --interval 5

# Stop current agent operation
juno agent stop

# Configure agent settings
juno agent configure --max-iterations 20 --temperature 0.7
```

### 5. Configuration Management

Manage application configuration via CLI:

```bash
# Show current configuration
juno config show --format json

# Set configuration values
juno config set --provider anthropic --model claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022

# Export configuration
juno config export --output config-backup.json

# Import configuration
juno config import --input config-backup.json

# Reset to defaults
juno config reset --confirm
```

### 6. System Operations

System health checks and diagnostics:

```bash
# System health check
juno system health --detailed --include-hardware

# Get system information
juno system info --hardware --permissions --connections

# Check permissions
juno system permissions --check --request-missing

# Performance monitoring
juno system monitor --duration 60 --interval 5

# Resource usage statistics
juno system stats --cpu --memory --disk
```

### 7. Batch Processing

Execute multiple commands efficiently:

```bash
# Execute commands from file
juno batch commands.txt --parallel 4 --continue-on-error

# Batch with custom settings
juno batch automation.txt --output json --timeout 900

# Batch with progress reporting
juno --verbose batch tasks.txt --progress --log batch-execution.log
```

**Example batch file (`commands.txt`):**

```
query "Take a screenshot"
system health --quick
voice record --duration 5 --output test.wav
query "Analyze the system status"
```

### 8. Interactive Mode

Real-time CLI session with the agent:

```bash
# Start interactive mode
juno interactive --format text --timeout 600

# Interactive with JSON output for scripting
juno interactive --output json --log session.log

# Interactive with voice support
juno interactive --enable-voice --voice-timeout 30
```

**Interactive commands:**

- `:help` - Show available commands
- `:status` - Show current system status
- `:voice` - Switch to voice input
- `:quit` or `:exit` - Exit interactive mode
- `:settings` - Show current settings
- Any other text - Execute as agent query

### 9. Daemon Mode

Background service operations:

```bash
# Start daemon in foreground
juno daemon start --foreground --log daemon.log

# Start daemon in background
juno daemon start --background --pid-file juno.pid

# Stop daemon
juno daemon stop --pid-file juno.pid

# Check daemon status
juno daemon status --pid-file juno.pid

# Daemon with health monitoring
juno daemon start --health-check-interval 300 --max-failures 3
```

### 10. Test Operations

Development and diagnostic testing:

```bash
# Run all tests
juno test all --report --output test-results.json

# Test specific components
juno test voice --duration 5
juno test accessibility --check-permissions
juno test tts --provider system --text "Hello world"

# Performance benchmarks
juno test performance --duration 60 --iterations 10

# Integration tests
juno test integration --suite basic --verbose
```

